zations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rahuldesirazu/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rahuldesirazu/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rahuldesirazu/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rahuldesirazu/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2022-05-18T20:57:37Z","updated_at":"2022-07-09T01:04:13Z","closed_at":"2022-06-29T20:14:50Z","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"Jira Link: [[DB-424]](https://yugabyte.atlassian.net/browse/DB-424)\r\n### Description\n\nWhen transactions are processed across multiple write batches/GetChanges calls, we see a data mismatch after transaction commit. This happens as a result of a bug on the target docdb side: For each row written to intentsdb, the format is `<txn_id, write_id> => key,value`, where write_id is an increasing counter to differentiate different rows of the same transaction. While write_id increases over a single write batch, it resets to 0 on the next write batch. Because we are writing to the same write_id across batches, we end up overwriting past rows written to intentsdb.\n\n[DB-424]: https://yugabyte.atlassian.net/browse/DB-424?atlOrigin=eyJpIjoiNWRkNTljNzYxNjVmNDY3MDlhMDU5Y2ZhYzA5YTRkZjUiLCJwIjoiZ2l0aHViLWNvbS1KU1cifQ","closed_by":{"login":"rahuldesirazu","id":7719567,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc3MTk1Njc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7719567?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rahuldesirazu","html_url":"https://github.com/rahuldesirazu","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rahuldesirazu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rahuldesirazu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.